# Private leak patterns (optional)

The public repo cannot list your employer's Jira project key, Slack channels, or
other tokens — that would defeat scrubbing.

Instead, maintain a **private** file on each machine:

```
~/.config/ai-skills/leak-patterns
```

Format: one extended regex per line. Lines starting with `#` are ignored.

Example (fill in with **your** values — do not commit this file):

```
# YOUR-PROJECT-[0-9]+
# #your-internal-channel
```

When pre-commit hooks exist in this repo, they load this file when present.

Generic patterns (corp Jira hosts, SharePoint personal URLs, `XXXX-1234`-shaped
keys) still run from the public hook without naming your organization.
